Therefore, hypoxia is one of the important manifestations of drunkenness. However, long-term alcoholics have developed a certain tolerance to alcohol and hypoxia, and they are basically unable to detect them when they are slightly drunk.
So, what principle does the smart wearable device use to detect blood oxygen saturation?
According to the medical definition, the oxygen saturation of the arterial blood of the human body is about 95%-100% under normal circumstances, and the oxygen saturation of the venous blood is about 75%. Generally, the arterial blood oxygen is less than 94% is insufficient oxygen supply, and less than 90% can be defined as hypoxemia.
For example, when performing mountaineering exercises at an altitude of 3000 meters or more, if the heart rate does not exceed 100, blood oxygen saturation greater than 90% is normal; 80%-90% is mild hypoxia, so you should reduce your activity , Proper rest; between 70%-80% is moderate hypoxia, appropriate oxygen should be inhaled, and anti-hypoxic drugs should be taken; less than 70% is severe hypoxia, all activities should be stopped, and medical treatment should be stopped.
