Step five: Design of the ejection system of the PVC pipe fitting mold.The ejection form of the product, the mechanical ejection is the last link in the injection molding process. The quality of the ejection will ultimately determine the quality of the product.
In order to prevent the product from deforming due to ejection, the thrust point should be as close as possible to the core or the part that is difficult to demold, such as the elongated hollow cylinder on the product, which is mostly ejected by the push tube. The arrangement of thrust points inside the PVC pipe moldshould be as balanced as possible.
The thrust point should act on the part where the product can withstand the greatest force, and the part with good rigidity, such as the interface of the Tee pipe fitting mold.
In order to make the force of the PVC pipe fittings uniform during ejection and avoid the deformation of the product due to vacuum adsorption, composite ejection or special forms of ejection systems are often used, such as push rods, push plates or push rods, and push pipes. Composite ejector, or use air intake push rod, push block and other setting devices, if necessary, an air intake valve should be set in the PVC pipe fitting mold.
