Because they are only engaged in one of the varieties, they may not know much about other molds, but we can learn more about the upstream and downstream of the mold industry by understanding the mold industry as a whole, so I All types of molds are classified.
During injection molding, the movable mold and the fixed mold are closed to form a pouring system and cavity.
Although the structure of the plastic mold may vary widely due to the variety and performance of the plastic, the shape and structure of the plastic product, and the type of injection machine, the basic structure is the same.
The combined part is called the parting line.
Molten metal can enter the mold from here, and the shape of this part matches the injection nozzle in the hot chamber die casting or the injection chamber in the cold chamber die casting.
The so-called runner is the channel between the gate and the cavity through which the molten metal enters the cavity.
The cavity is divided into two cavity inserts, which are independent parts that can be removed or installed from the mold relatively easily by bolts.
In this way, the push rod of the movable part will push the casting out.
It will accurately drive all the push rods at the same time with the same amount of force, so as to ensure that the casting is not damaged.
Since the casting is still at a high temperature when it is demolded, only the number of push rods is large enough to ensure that the average pressure on each push rod is small enough to not damage the casting.
Other parts in the mold include core slides and so on.
They can also be used to increase the details of the casting.
The direction of the fixed core is parallel to the direction of the casting out of the mold.
The movable core can be arranged in any direction except the ejection direction.
The slider and the movable core are very close, the biggest difference is that the slider can be used to make an undercut surface.
Loose cores are also called take-out blocks and can be used to make complex surfaces, such as threaded holes.
The runner is part of the molding material, but it is not a product.
This is the ideal situation, but it is difficult to achieve the best of both worlds in practical applications.
Since there is a heating rod and a heating ring near or in the center of the runner, the entire runner from the nozzle exit of the injection molding machine to the gate is in a high temperature state, so that the plastic in the runner is kept molten.
When starting the machine, you only need to heat the runner to the required temperature.
