The name of THE HOLY LAND OF VIET NAM STUDIES derives from emotion in many researchers of Vietnam studies who live in Vietnam and in foreign countries.
As identified in the Vietnamese context, the Holy land of Vietnam has soon transformed into an industry of academy named Vietnam with a network spreading many countries and territories of the world. Formerly, the network of Viet Nam Studies considered Europe, especially France, Japan, China and the United States of America as places where there have been contributions to the Vietnamese history written commonly.
There was an international symposium on Viet Nam studies in Vietnam in 1988 which made Euro–Viet identified as an academic industry orientating the motherland. It was the place that has generated people with a cultural value not being dimmed when standing with the same industries, if not brightening, for instance, Japan studies Korea studies, Southeast Asia studies.
