With a population of about 12,095 persons, the LA CHI chiefly live in Xin Man District (Ha Giang Province) and Muong Khuong and Bac Ha Districts (Lao Cai Province1). Their other names are Cu Te and La Qua.
The LA CHI live in villages, in which each family owns a house-on-stilts as the living quarter and an adjoining house on the ground as the kitchen. The house-on-stilts has three compartments and the only stairway near the kitchen.
La Chi women used to carry a papoose ever their forehead, no matter it is made of cloth or bamboo plaits, while men carry shoulder dossers. Each family lineage has its own drums and gongs used in ritual ceremonies.
There are many old tales about the founder of this ethnic group-old HOANG DIN THUNG about PU LO TO who created different genera and species and taught people habits and customs, and about natural phenomena. Young boys and girls like to sing ni ca songs.
