The “collaborators”: A lot of Vietnamese voluntarily worked for the French authority under ranks of mercenaries, such as the “Mã Tà” (Matas). To the Chinese communities in Saigon, the French conquest of Cochinchina brought them more benefits than before as they actively collaborated with the “new authority” (In contrast, the Sino-Vietnamese communities in Rạch Giá Province and Phú Quốc Island actively joined the resistance movements of Nguyễn Trung Trực in 1868).
The conflicts between the Vietnamese Catholics and Vietnamese Confucianists: In 1874, the Confucianists in Central Vietnam blamed the Vietnamese Catholics for the collaborations and the lost of Southern Vietnam to the French forces. Therefore, the uprising was happened with the slogan of“Bình Tây Sát Tả!”(Pacify the French, Kill the Heresies!).
