To contextualize this statement, it should be mentioned that Chile currently has 17.5 million hectares (ha) of forest: 82 percent natural forest, 17 percent plantations (mainly pines and eucalyptus) and 1 percent mixed production.
In fact, of the total energy consumed for heating, 81 percent comes from firewood, which means that around 1.7 million households in Chile currently use this fuel, reaching a total annual consumption of over 11.7 million m³ of wood. More efficient alternatives
